# Ruling 2020-09-25: if the target land is illegal on resolution the spell does not resolve (CR 608.2b) - no search, no draw. Bot2
# sacrifices the targeted Ghost Quarter in response (its cost), destroying Bot1's tapped Mountain; Bot1 declines that
# search. Wildfire fizzles: Bot1's hand stays at 7 - 2 lands + 1 draw - Wildfire = 5, and Bot2 is never asked to search.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Cleansing Wildfire
Mountain x4
Mountain x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Ghost Quarter
Island x6
Forest
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ghost Quarter.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cleansing Wildfire.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ghost Quarter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ghost Quarter.Activate(Ability: Destroy; Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1)
Bot1.Decline

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ghost Quarter
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Cleansing Wildfire; Mountain
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain
Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
